# cloudflared with its tunnel token read from SSM at startup, for the Cloudflare MCP portal
# tunnel in front of this server's profiles (docs/tool-profiles.md, "portal"; deployed by
# terraform-helm modules/cloudflared-mcp-portal).
#
# One container, no init container and no Kubernetes secret: scripts/cloudflared/entrypoint.py
# reads the token with the pod's IRSA role, writes it to an in-memory file and execs
# cloudflared with the container's arguments. Without TUNNEL_TOKEN_PARAMETER it runs
# cloudflared as is.
#
#   docker build -f Dockerfile.cloudflared -t cloudflared-mcp-portal .
#   docker run --rm cloudflared-mcp-portal version
#
# Jenkins builds it like Dockerfile.production, in its own ECR repository
# (exploit/cloudflared-mcp-portal). To upgrade cloudflared, change CLOUDFLARED_VERSION.

ARG CLOUDFLARED_VERSION=2026.10.7

# Cloudflare's image, for its binary only (static, also on distroless Debian 13).
FROM cloudflare/cloudflared:${CLOUDFLARED_VERSION} AS cloudflared

# boto3 and its dependencies, pinned with hashes, for the runtime's Python (3.13).
FROM python:3.13-slim-trixie AS deps
COPY scripts/cloudflared/requirements.txt /tmp/requirements.txt
RUN pip install \
        --no-cache-dir \
        --disable-pip-version-check \
        --root-user-action=ignore \
        --require-hashes \
        --only-binary=:all: \
        --target /opt/entrypoint-deps \
        -r /tmp/requirements.txt


FROM gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian13:nonroot

ENV PYTHONPATH=/opt/entrypoint-deps \
    PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 \
    NO_AUTOUPDATE=true

COPY --from=cloudflared /usr/local/bin/cloudflared /usr/local/bin/cloudflared
COPY --from=deps /opt/entrypoint-deps /opt/entrypoint-deps
COPY scripts/cloudflared/entrypoint.py /opt/entrypoint.py

# distroless "nonroot", also the owner of the token file.
USER 65532:65532

ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/bin/python3", "/opt/entrypoint.py"]
CMD ["version"]
